@startuml

header "Video processing after send (doc 29 Phases 7–9)"
footer "Source: docs/logs/29_user-upload-video-24mb.md\nCaptured WS: PROCESSING_PENDING then MEDIA_READY\nWorker never publishes WebSocket"

actor "Group members\n(STOMP /topic/group.5)" as Clients
participant "chat-app-backend" as Backend
database "PostgreSQL\n(messages, message_media)" as DB
participant "RabbitMQ\nmedia.processing" as Jobs
participant "media-processing-service" as Worker
participant "MinIO\n(chat-media)" as MinIO
participant "Realtime\n(STOMP + chat.groups)" as Realtime

note over Clients, Realtime
  Starts **after** prepare / multipart / complete have already persisted
  message 213634 + attachment 84 (VIDEO, original .mov, SCAN_PASSED).
  This diagram is the doc 29 path only.
end note

== 1. After complete commit: first WebSocket message ==

Backend -> Backend: AfterCommit:\n1) publish MessageResponse snapshot\n2) enqueueProcessing(messageId)

Backend -> Realtime: publishToGroup(5, MessageResponse)
Realtime -> Clients: **WS #1** same payload for every member\n(including sender)

note over Clients
  WS #1 — attachment.status = PROCESSING_PENDING
  playbackUrl / contentUrl / videoSources[CANONICAL]
  still point at the original .mov
  posterUrl = null, no MOBILE source yet
end note

Backend -> Jobs: MediaProcessingJobMessage\nexchange=media.processing\nroutingKey=media.processing.video\nqueue=media.processing.jobs\njobId=media-84\ntargets=METADATA, THUMBNAIL, TRANSCODE

note over Backend, Jobs
  Enqueue is skipped if MEDIA_PROCESSING_ENABLED=false.
  The worker does **not** send this (or any) WebSocket.
end note

== 2. Worker consumes and writes derivatives (no WS) ==

Jobs -> Worker: deliver job (RabbitMQ consumer)
Worker -> MinIO: GET original objectKey (.mov)
Worker -> Worker: ffprobe METADATA\nffmpeg poster → {stem}.thumbnail.jpg\nffmpeg TRANSCODE → {stem}.transcoded.mp4\noptional 480p → {stem}.480p.mp4

Worker -> MinIO: PUT thumbnail.jpg
Worker -> MinIO: PUT transcoded.mp4
Worker -> MinIO: PUT 480p.mp4\n(skip if already ≤480p / too short / too small;\n480p failure does not fail MEDIA_READY)

note over Worker
  One callback at the end of the job.
  Happy path here: pendingTargets=[] → status=MEDIA_READY.
  No PROCESSING_IN_PROGRESS WebSocket in this capture.
end note

Worker -> Backend: POST /api/internal/media-processing/results\nX-Media-Processing-Token\nstatus=MEDIA_READY\nthumbnailObjectKey, transcodedObjectKey,\nvideoMetadata, videoRenditions[{480p}]

== 3. Backend applies result: second WebSocket message ==

Backend -> DB: lock MessageMedia 84\nwrite width/height/durationMs,\nthumbnail, canonical keys, 480p key\nstatus=MEDIA_READY\nobjectKey := transcoded.mp4

Backend -> Backend: AfterCommit:\n1) map MessageResponse + presigned URLs\n2) delete replaced original .mov

Backend -> Realtime: publishToGroup(5, MessageResponse)
Realtime -> Clients: **WS #2** same message id 213634

note over Clients
  WS #2 — attachment.status = MEDIA_READY
  mimeType=video/mp4, duration/width/height set
  playbackUrl / downloadUrl / contentUrl = transcoded.mp4
  posterUrl = thumbnail.jpg
  videoSources:
    CANONICAL = transcoded.mp4 (3024×1964)
    MOBILE = 480p.mp4 (740×480)
end note

Backend -> MinIO: DELETE original .mov\n(after commit; only if not reused)
Worker -> Jobs: ACK job\n(after HTTP 204; failed callback → redelivery)

@enduml
